Trajectory geometry propagates NaN, which changes results that had missing time points. A gap used to count as a zero-length step, so path length and AUC speed came out finite and too small; they are now NaN, as are curvature, cohesion, intra-spread and Mahalanobis separation at the gap, and every `TrajectoryResult` summary that uses the missing point (mean and max speed, curvature, cohesion, separation peak and AUC used to skip it). `TrajectoryResult` no longer casts condition labels to int: labels such as `3.0` or `"3"` stay as given, which changes pair names (`"3.0_vs_4.0"`) and keys; cast them before building the result to keep the old ones.
